Cell["\<\
This reveals the framework's ultimate routing safeguard: the dispatcher uses \
the wavepacket's type to securely route the exact same user string to \
completely different backend evaluation symbols (e.g., GWP1DHARMONIC versus \
GWPCTHARMONIC).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998588515838118*^9, {3.9986039395945063`*^9, 3.998603942521584*^9}},
 CellID->1329069758,ExpressionUUID->"da8214fa-c4ad-4e53-9cef-e9c09a056dc6"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Multi-Tier Dispatcher & Signature Routing", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9986055348985147`*^9, 3.9986055393801327`*^9}},
 CellID->1431811971,ExpressionUUID->"4e561b25-07e0-4b95-bd7e-e2f7cc566aaf"],

Cell["\<\
The GWPDispatcher.wl package serves as a multi-tier firewall and polymorphic \
router. It isolates the frontend user from the developer backend while \
ensuring every mathematical operation is automatically constructed with the \
correct wavepacket type and time-dependence.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9985114434679403`*^9, 3.998575244579138*^9, {3.998604688239091*^9, 
   3.998604691271201*^9}},
 CellID->1210568855,ExpressionUUID->"a3f70173-4ba5-46e8-9ca8-9ed4a8197588"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tier 1: The Factory Architecture:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " When the GWP constructor is called, the dispatcher intercepts the \
\"Potential\" option. It references the unified $GWPPotentials database to \
silently map the cosmetic string (e.g., \"Free\") to a protected developer \
evaluation symbol."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998575841498612*^9},
 CellID->1221382916,ExpressionUUID->"793bdfd4-f099-4d15-bbbb-68564ff6210d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Examine the internal state of a static versus a dynamic wavepacket. \
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998511515671195*^9, 3.9985115590805387`*^9}, 
   3.99857532912843*^9, 3.998605455988742*^9},
 CellID->1439158868,ExpressionUUID->"43c1b94f-b367-4e74-83f0-e829497179fc"],

