Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Math Engines & The Parameter Bus", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998523181146459*^9, 3.998523192161284*^9}},
 CellID->10482156,ExpressionUUID->"c80cba26-d07c-4f68-a954-901d0a870170"],

Cell["\<\
The computational engines (e.g., GWPEngine1D.wl, GWPEngineCT.wl) contain the \
raw algebraic evaluators for physical observables and time-evolution \
propagators. To guarantee compatibility with the Dispatcher, every engine is \
constructed using a strict structural blueprint centered around a \
macro-expansion strategy known as the Parameter Bus.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998550842814509*^9, 3.99855085411447*^9}, 
   3.9985759922145357`*^9, 3.998580158629869*^9, 3.9986111207495527`*^9},
 CellID->938767742,ExpressionUUID->"d3e9281e-e8a9-47e3-b8c9-695989d54f06"],

Cell["\<\
To illustrate the entire lifecycle\[LongDash]from usage registration to the \
parameter bus, function definition, and low-level evaluation\[LongDash]the \
Classical Trajectory (CT) engine is deconstructed below.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998580166508711*^9, {3.998581599251145*^9, 3.998581619460758*^9}, 
   3.9986111330173283`*^9},
 CellID->672507025,ExpressionUUID->"9133e293-af76-4136-a3d0-3c14d5fc9bda"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Step 1: Usage Registration (Symbol Hoisting)", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9985232545873013`*^9, 3.998523273697029*^9}, 
   3.998576029068928*^9},
 CellID->307085285,ExpressionUUID->"4befb9cb-39b0-494b-86dd-84dde82b68fd"],

Cell["\<\
Before an engine defines its private mathematical logic, it fetches the \
shared dictionary using Needs (ensuring the file is only read from disk once \
per session) and temporarily opens the developer context to declare its \
specific macros.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.999552252778295*^9},
 CellID->186127593,ExpressionUUID->"0413028c-d224-40cf-a760-e15dc4ac5aa7"],

Cell["\<\
To guarantee a completely silent initialization sequence that respects the \
user's workspace, the engine explicitly turns off shadowing warnings \
(Off[General::shdw]) while injecting these symbols. Telemetry hooks \
($GWPDebug) are also included at the boundaries to allow developers to trace \
the package loading order.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.999552285503338*^9},
 CellID->1510265519,ExpressionUUID->"a2d48331-f222-4baf-a58f-0afe6d1d8d88"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Once the symbols are hoisted, Quiet is used to safely close the package \
block, and the developer context is explicitly scrubbed from the global \
$ContextPath. This prevents the developer namespace from polluting the global \
environment while ensuring the symbols remain defined for the engine's \
internal logic.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9995523260790157`*^9},
 CellID->1923353940,ExpressionUUID->"ae3e770a-aa40-4952-921c-4107856cbbb4"],

Cell["\<\
(* ========================================================================= *)
(* Usage Registration (Symbol Hoisting)                                      *)
(* ========================================================================= *)
Needs[\"GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\"];
BeginPackage[\"GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\"]

If[TrueQ[Global`$GWPDebug], Print[\"[GWPEngineCT] BeginPackage \
GWPDeveloper\"]];

(* Suppress shadowing warnings during the silent boot sequence *)
Off[General::shdw];

(* Parameter Bus Macros *)
GWPCTARG::usage = \"Macro for Classical Trajectory argument pattern.\";
GWPCTVAL::usage = \"Macro for Classical Trajectory values.\";

(* Constructor *)
GWPCTPARAM::usage = \"GWPCTPARAM[x0, p0] generates the Classical Trajectory \
parameter sequence.\";

(* Properties *)
GWPCTRX::usage = \"Extracts the classical position.\";
GWPCTRP::usage = \"Extracts the classical momentum.\";
GWPCTKE::usage = \"Evaluates the classical kinetic energy.\";
GWPCTPE::usage = \"Evaluates the classical potential energy.\";
GWPCTTE::usage = \"Evaluates the classical total energy.\";

(* Potentials *)
GWPCTFREE::usage     = \"Propagator for a classical free particle.\";
GWPCTHARMONIC::usage = \"Propagator for a classical harmonic oscillator.\";

If[TrueQ[Global`$GWPDebug], Print[\"[GWPEngineCT] EndPackage GWPDeveloper\"]];

Quiet[EndPackage[], General::shdw]
$ContextPath = DeleteCases[$ContextPath, \"GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\"];\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998576196555159*^9, 3.998580209363208*^9, {3.998580474652698*^9, 
   3.998580478250474*^9}, 3.999552228092424*^9, 4.000412000992323*^9},
 CellID->619135014,ExpressionUUID->"942f154e-c62e-4d97-b17c-11771f47d838"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Step 2: Private Engine Logic & Dependencies", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9985802259881363`*^9, 3.998580246657795*^9}},
 CellID->1414578560,ExpressionUUID->"0b6fbf3c-e55c-4bba-9cae-00667390cf70"],

Cell["\<\
After hoisting symbols, the engine opens its own isolated Private context. \
Proper loading order within this block is critical: if the engine depends on \
mathematical evaluators from other engines (e.g., GWPEngine1D), those \
dependencies must be loaded via Needs before loading GWPDeveloper and \
GWPRegistry. This strict internal routing prevents symbol shadowing and \
ensures the framework shares a unified vocabulary. As with the symbol \
hoisting block, telemetry hooks are placed at the boundaries to allow \
developers to trace the initialization of the private scope.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.999552455779323*^9},
 CellID->1135560589,ExpressionUUID->"4fcf93c7-ca2e-44cc-8f53-5d9c415c1eb2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
At the conclusion of the file, the ReadProtected attribute is applied to all \
symbols within the engine's namespace. This hides the internal code from \
Mathematica's ? introspection menu, maintaining a clean interface.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.999552466890904*^9},
 CellID->679648434,ExpressionUUID->"211e0641-70ab-439f-b632-9472dd5fc339"],

Cell["\<\
(* ========================================================================= *)
(* Private Engine Logic & Registration                                       *)
(* ========================================================================= *)
BeginPackage[\"GWPTools`GWPEngineCT`\"];
If[TrueQ[Global`$GWPDebug], Print[\"[GWPEngineCT] BeginPackage\"]];

Begin[\"`Private`\"];
If[TrueQ[Global`$GWPDebug], Print[\"[GWPEngineCT] Begin Private\"]];

Needs[\"GWPTools`GWPDeveloper`\"];
Needs[\"GWPTools`GWPRegistry`\"];

  (* ... Body of Code (Parameters, Functions, Potentials, Registry) ... *)

If[TrueQ[Global`$GWPDebug], Print[\"[GWPEngineCT] End Private\"]];
End[];

(* Hide internal code for all Developer functions from the ? menu *)
SetAttributes[Evaluate[Names[\"GWPTools`GWPEngineCT`*\"]], {ReadProtected}];

If[TrueQ[Global`$GWPDebug], Print[\"[GWPEngineCT] EndPackage\"]];
EndPackage[];\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998580300130864*^9, {3.9985804830097837`*^9, 3.9985804896852007`*^9}, 
   3.999552514304908*^9, {4.000412061546872*^9, 4.000412085281664*^9}},
 CellID->2143687575,ExpressionUUID->"733b1282-e5af-4142-b200-3ccbaebd3605"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The subsequent steps (Steps 3 through 6) detail the core logic that populates \
the body of this package.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->443628216,ExpressionUUID->"9f39ab1c-7dc1-4227-8549-1f82f9cee980"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Step 3: The Parameter Bus & Constructor", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998523325264298*^9, 3.9985233420199337`*^9}, {
  3.9985762887060843`*^9, 3.9985763047267313`*^9}, {3.998580325930759*^9, 
  3.998580326326195*^9}},
 CellID->988459602,ExpressionUUID->"863afec8-74ac-4575-a614-492ce8567563"],

Cell["\<\
Every engine defines two paired macros. GWPtypeARG is a sequence of patterns \
used strictly on the left-hand side of definitions to define the mathematical \
signature. GWPtypeVAL is a sequence of bound symbols used on the right-hand \
side to pass evaluated parameters downstream.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9985233807324*^9, 3.99857631635544*^9, 
  3.998580350649692*^9},
 CellID->107037622,ExpressionUUID->"2aa45a4b-a4cf-466d-a160-e61999037727"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Because the CT engine tracks a classical point particle, its Parameter Bus is \
highly streamlined: it isolates position (RX), momentum (RP), mass (MASS), \
local potential coefficients (V0, V1, V2), and time-origin metadata (INIT). \
The constructor parses external inputs, enforces real-valued coordinates, and \
generates this exact sequence.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9985509434782267`*^9, 3.9985509460834513`*^9}, 
   3.998576327761685*^9, 3.998580359395578*^9},
 CellID->167034977,ExpressionUUID->"6a83b8aa-94ef-4dea-9adc-2f39ca4a78b8"],

Cell["\<\
(* --- Parameter Bus Definition --- *)
GWPCTARG = Sequence[RX_, RP_, MASS_, {V0_, V1_, V2_}, INIT_];
GWPCTVAL = Sequence[RX, RP, MASS, {V0, V1, V2}, INIT];

(* --- Constructor Engine --- *)
Options[GWPCTPARAM] = {\"MASS\" -> 1};

GWPCTPARAM[X0_, P0_, opts : OptionsPattern[]] := Module[{rx, rp, m},
  (* Enforce real-valued coordinates and extract mass *)
  rx = ComplexExpand[Re[X0]];
  rp = ComplexExpand[Re[P0]];
  m  = OptionValue[\"MASS\"];

  (* Output the initialized Parameter Bus *)
  (* Format: {RX, RP, MASS, PECOEFF, INIT} *)
  Sequence @@ {rx, rp, m, {0, 0, 0}, {rx, rp}}
];
\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998576390066882*^9, 3.998580371275543*^9, {3.998580438480297*^9, 
   3.99858043936464*^9}, {3.998580496243606*^9, 3.998580499612432*^9}, 
   4.000412114368988*^9},
 CellID->814405429,ExpressionUUID->"df369c8e-37a9-4464-82f0-78edd1f7c5bc"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Generating a raw parameter sequence using the engine's constructor \
demonstrates how the outputs perfectly align with the GWPCTVAL sequence \
structure.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998611514500844*^9, 3.998611515444747*^9}, {
  3.9986115948046627`*^9, 3.9986115952456303`*^9}},
 CellID->969893812,ExpressionUUID->"e8d64b2f-3d7f-46eb-b791-9bd8b3d9db10"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["GWPCTVAL"], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998611572758906*^9, 3.998611578647859*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[31]:=",
 CellID->12340898,ExpressionUUID->"78f7785d-9a50-48a6-a1a4-cd85e18d163e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Sequence", "[", 
  RowBox[{"RX", ",", "RP", ",", "MASS", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"V0", ",", "V1", ",", "V2"}], "}"}], ",", "INIT"}], 
  "]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.99861157987437*^9, 3.998612204886064*^9, 
  4.000412250360167*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[31]=",
 CellID->259303356,ExpressionUUID->"2d042ec1-025f-4f8e-b725-d3fb65fbddff"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"GWPCTPARAM", "[", 
  RowBox[{"RX", ",", "RP", ",", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<MASS\>\"", "->", "MASS"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998576462310988*^9, 3.998576485658613*^9}, {
  3.998580803842351*^9, 3.998580821473927*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[32]:=",
 CellID->694981874,ExpressionUUID->"f6548530-015b-47a1-ad04-4e402a8cf359"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Sequence", "[", 
  RowBox[{"RX", ",", "RP", ",", "MASS", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"RX", ",", "RP"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9985817137687597`*^9, 3.99861158176066*^9, 
  3.99861220490598*^9, 4.000412250368042*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[32]=",
 CellID->867184529,ExpressionUUID->"72c314b7-9d1d-4611-a1d4-d7d30aafe4e3"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Step 4: Static Function Definitions & Passing the Bus", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998576520456058*^9, 3.998576542030864*^9}, {
  3.998580328951844*^9, 3.9985803294512444`*^9}},
 CellID->1888549093,ExpressionUUID->"9119d86c-b0b0-4280-aeb5-edb43fdb9738"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
With the bus established, the engine defines its physical observables. Simple \
properties unpack the sequence directly to perform calculations. When \
building a higher-order composite property (like Total Energy) that relies on \
evaluating other base properties, the Parameter Bus must be explicitly passed \
downstream. By wrapping the definition in With[{val = GWPCTVAL}, ...], the \
evaluated sequence is safely injected into the right-hand side without \
breaking the delayed evaluation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998550964139449*^9, 3.998550974342634*^9}, 
   3.9985765535952806`*^9, 3.99858040648603*^9},
 CellID->595731810,ExpressionUUID->"b70ebceb-bbb6-4226-9750-6b59eda8d44b"],

Cell["\<\
(* --- Static Function Definitions --- *)
(* GWPCTARG unpacks the sequence to define the exact signature *)
GWPCTRX[GWPCTARG] = RX;
GWPCTRP[GWPCTARG] = RP;
GWPCTKE[GWPCTARG] = RP^2 / (2 * MASS);
GWPCTPE[GWPCTARG] = V0 + V1 * RX + V2 * RX^2;

(* Passing the bus downstream requires With to inject GWPCTVAL *)
With[{val = GWPCTVAL}, 
  GWPCTTE[GWPCTARG] := GWPCTKE[val] + GWPCTPE[val]
];\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9985765764260798`*^9, {3.998580427022635*^9, 3.998580444968358*^9}, {
   3.998580504611496*^9, 3.9985805049550123`*^9}, 4.00041213776296*^9},
 CellID->692839336,ExpressionUUID->"68a56b9a-4e0f-4e45-866e-ecb478c823d2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Apply the raw sequence directly to the protected function heads to bypass the \
frontend router and perform the exact algebraic calculations instantly.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9986116773317327`*^9},
 CellID->894386118,ExpressionUUID->"2ee147d1-a33e-4a21-8596-b909fa52a531"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"PARAM", "=", 
   RowBox[{"GWPCTPARAM", "[", 
    RowBox[{"RX", ",", "RP", ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<MASS\>\"", "->", "MASS"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"GWPCTRX", "@", "PARAM"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"GWPCTKE", "@", "PARAM"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998576600132353*^9, {3.998578132064705*^9, 3.998578132343156*^9}, {
   3.99858099661902*^9, 3.998581024414131*^9}, {3.998581063797945*^9, 
   3.99858108274688*^9}, {3.998611685210761*^9, 3.998611686284594*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[33]:=",
 CellID->1709439873,ExpressionUUID->"801041ab-6bcf-43d0-826d-f136750c8515"],

Cell[BoxData["RX"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998581713783722*^9, 3.998611689192913*^9, 
  3.9986122049142933`*^9, 4.000412250396657*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[34]=",
 CellID->1946350361,ExpressionUUID->"08c3f816-0b52-4e33-80b7-c6f7c6832780"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox[
  SuperscriptBox["RP", "2"], 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", "MASS"}]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998581713783722*^9, 3.998611689192913*^9, 
  3.9986122049142933`*^9, 4.0004122503974733`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[35]=",
 CellID->1839606223,ExpressionUUID->"2fbd1c1a-6985-4b68-9474-ea6baadba32d"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Step 5: Potential Models & Time Evolution", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998576656549677*^9, 3.998576666613717*^9}, {
  3.998580332146057*^9, 3.998580332497334*^9}},
 CellID->1418239864,ExpressionUUID->"0031da26-51ec-4c54-a779-f2f551cee8a0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
While standard observables return an algebraic value, a potential model must \
actively advance the dynamic parameters forward in time. A valid potential \
function takes time t and the parameter bus, computes the evolved kinematics, \
updates the local potential energy coefficients, and explicitly returns a \
newly reconstructed Sequence.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->184239376,ExpressionUUID->"e2e10066-c509-4bee-bc2b-f5eb56d9f8fe"],

Cell["\<\
(* --- Potential Propagators --- *)
GWPCTFREE[t_][GWPCTARG] := Module[{newRX, newRP, newV},
  newRX = RX + (RP / MASS) * t;
  newRP = RP; 
  newV  = {0, 0, 0}; 
  Sequence @@ {newRX, newRP, MASS, newV, INIT}
];

GWPCTHARMONIC[omega_][t_][GWPCTARG] := Module[{newRX, newRP, newV},
  newRX = RX * Cos[omega * t] + (RP / (MASS * omega)) * Sin[omega * t];
  newRP = RP * Cos[omega * t] - MASS * omega * RX * Sin[omega * t]; 
  newV  = {0, 0, 1/2 * MASS * omega^2}; 
  Sequence @@ {newRX, newRP, MASS, newV, INIT}
];\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998576686335936*^9, {3.998580508967009*^9, 3.9985805093236847`*^9}, {
   3.998580555538055*^9, 3.998580558455377*^9}, 4.0004121564509706`*^9},
 CellID->478750862,ExpressionUUID->"2842ce8e-463e-46a0-9900-f0c43b1fcfb9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the harmonic potential to observe the reconstructed sequence, then \
feed it directly into the static position property (GWPCTRX) to extract the \
time-dependent dynamics.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.998580572795603*^9, {3.998611778621661*^9, 3.998611797736067*^9}},
 CellID->1891995972,ExpressionUUID->"b400d71c-eed9-4202-bc39-2550ab31586e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GWPCTHARMONIC", "[", "OMEGA", "]"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "[", 
  "PARAM", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998576719954494*^9, 3.998576752755975*^9}, {
   3.998578202702545*^9, 3.998578204227393*^9}, {3.998580784432042*^9, 
   3.9985807876216908`*^9}, {3.998581119252543*^9, 3.99858112996694*^9}, 
   3.998581667185009*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[36]:=",
 CellID->714381673,ExpressionUUID->"8179c95b-1db4-46e4-becd-c42e01a606de"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Sequence", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RX", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"OMEGA", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"RP", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"OMEGA", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"MASS", " ", "OMEGA"}]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RP", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"OMEGA", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"MASS", " ", "OMEGA", " ", "RX", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"OMEGA", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "MASS", ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"MASS", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["OMEGA", "2"]}], "2"]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"RX", ",", "RP"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998581713803668*^9, 3.998611802224331*^9, 
  3.9986122049314137`*^9, 4.000412250415616*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[36]=",
 CellID->939724102,ExpressionUUID->"dfcb8165-6672-4c83-afb2-f6a61ec18f2a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
